# Dogear runs fully offline with no configuration: accounts, saves and the whole book library
# live on the device. Set these two to point the same app at a real Supabase project instead.
#
#   1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com
#   2. Run the migrations in supabase/migrations (supabase db push, or paste them in order
#      into the SQL editor)
#   3. Load the content:  npm run content:all  then run supabase/seed.sql
#   4. Copy this file to .env and fill in the two values below from Project Settings → API
#
# Both are EXPO_PUBLIC_, meaning they are inlined into the client bundle. That is correct for
# the anon key — it is designed to be public, and row level security is what actually protects
# the data. Never put the service_role key in this file.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
